# me-ai — Architecture

**Browser-only AI assistant built on an event-stream model.**
No backend server. The LLM runs entirely in the browser via WebGPU or Ollama, and Gmail/Twitter use client-side OAuth.

**Never use fallback functionality — strictly prohibited.** Do not implement or rely on fallback paths, default alternatives, or degradation; fail explicitly when the primary path is unavailable.

## Knowledge base: `.cortex/`

The repository knowledge base lives in `.cortex/`. See **[`.cortex/index.md`](.cortex/index.md)** for the full knowledge base and agent role index.

## Project layout

- **me-ai-core** (Rust, WASM) — Business logic, persistence (IndexedDB via Rexie), plugins, LLM. Exposes WASM API via `MeAiCore` in `lib.rs`. See `.cortex/architecture.md` for module layout.
- **me-ai-web** (Svelte 5 + TypeScript) — Frontend and app layer. Depends on `me-ai-core` as a local package (`file:../me-ai-core/pkg`).

**Building, installing, testing, and deploying** must go through the **builder** subagent.
Do not run `npm install`, `npm run build`, or `task` from the repo root yourself; use the builder.
All Taskfile tasks and workflow are defined in `.agents/me-ai-builder.md`.
